NASEER MOHAMMAD: Sure, go ahead.

00:37:01.550 --> 00:37:06.320
CHRIS PAGE: Why isn't the client
authenticated before the threat

00:37:06.320 --> 00:37:08.680
protections?

00:37:08.680 --> 00:37:10.270
I guess-- I think
the way I interpret

00:37:10.270 --> 00:37:14.320
it is, why is the client not
identified before the threat

00:37:14.320 --> 00:37:17.890
protections are
implemented or exercised?

00:37:17.890 --> 00:37:21.050
Well, in the real world,
API security best practices,

00:37:21.050 --> 00:37:24.040
yes, the client really
should be authenticated

00:37:24.040 --> 00:37:27.550
before inspecting that
payload queries, et cetera,

00:37:27.550 --> 00:37:31.090
to identify really which
client and what client

00:37:31.090 --> 00:37:33.340
is sending the malicious data.

00:37:33.340 --> 00:37:36.760
Best practices are fail
fast before requiring

00:37:36.760 --> 00:37:41.380
additional system resources
for inspection of the request

00:37:41.380 --> 00:37:43.171
payload.

00:37:43.171 --> 00:37:45.040
Typically, AuthN
or AuthZ will be

00:37:45.040 --> 00:37:49.450
covered in a future "Apigee Up
Close" and security webinar.

00:37:49.450 --> 00:37:51.170
How can you monitor--

00:37:51.170 --> 00:37:54.220
next question, how can you
monitor malicious clients

00:37:54.220 --> 00:37:57.280
in pattern matching
or rule-based filters?

00:37:57.280 --> 00:37:58.820
That's a great one.

00:37:58.820 --> 00:38:01.810
Apigee does have a product
called Apigee Sense, which

00:38:01.810 --> 00:38:03.520
does specifically that.

00:38:03.520 --> 00:38:07.600
It applies adaptive
API security product

00:38:07.600 --> 00:38:09.665
to mitigate sophisticated
bot attacks.

00:38:09.665 --> 00:38:14.350
It leverages machine learning
and detects anomalies

00:38:14.350 --> 00:38:17.700
based off pattern
matching at the API layer.

00:38:17.700 --> 00:38:22.240
[INAUDIBLE] the ability to
create dynamic rules or custom

00:38:22.240 --> 00:38:25.660
rules based off of
that pattern matching

00:38:25.660 --> 00:38:27.910
that the product provides.

00:38:27.910 --> 00:38:31.090
Also enables you to take
action on those bots

00:38:31.090 --> 00:38:32.720
you find, whether
it be throttle,

00:38:32.720 --> 00:38:34.540
block, log, et cetera.

00:38:34.540 --> 00:38:38.915
And we also have another
